{
  "_readme": [
    "Colour literal -> design token. This table is the reviewable artifact of the",
    "theme migration: reading it tells you exactly what the codemod will do,",
    "without reading thousands of diffs.",
    "",
    "Every entry was chosen from the actual frequency histogram of the codebase,",
    "not invented. Each hex below is used for essentially ONE semantic role (e.g.",
    "#9ca3af is `color:` 661 times and `borderColor:` twice), which is what makes",
    "a blind string substitution safe here.",
    "",
    "Keys are normalised before lookup: hex is lowercased, rgb/rgba has all",
    "whitespace stripped. So '#06B6D4' and '#06b6d4' are one key, and",
    "'rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.15)' and 'rgba(6,182,212,0.15)' are one key.",
    "",
    "NOT a place for board/piece colours — those are chess CONTENT and are",
    "excluded by path in tokenize.mjs."
  ],

